SentinelLog Commercial EULA (For Enterprise Customers)

SentinelLog End User License Agreement (EULA)
Effective Date: January 1, 2025
Issued by: SentinelLog Technologies Inc., associated with Gemra Ventures

This EULA governs all licensed on-premise or downloadable versions of SentinelLog.

Grant of License

SentinelLog grants the customer a non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to install and use SentinelLog within their organization.

Restrictions

The customer may not:
• reverse engineer, decompile, or attempt to extract source code
• redistribute or sublicense SentinelLog
• provide access to non-employees without written consent
• modify or create derivative works
• benchmark or compare publicly without approval

Ownership

SentinelLog remains the exclusive property of
SentinelLog Technologies Inc.
Naveen Sajeendran and Midunan Sivasaravanan retain all intellectual property rights.

Confidentiality

All documentation, source code elements, algorithms, threat models, and detection rules are proprietary confidential information.

Termination

If the customer violates this EULA, the license terminates immediately.

SentinelLog SaaS Terms of Service (For hosted cloud customers)

SentinelLog Cloud Terms of Service
Operated by SentinelLog Technologies Inc., associated with Gemra Ventures

Use of Service

Users receive access to the hosted SentinelLog platform for log ingestion, threat detection, dashboards, and alerts.

Customer Responsibilities

• Not upload malware or harmful content
• Not exceed rate limits
• Not misuse SentinelLog to attack third parties

Data Rights

Customers retain ownership of their uploaded logs.
SentinelLog owns all analytics, detection models, and derived insights.

Service Level

SentinelLog targets 99.5 percent uptime. Outages may occur. No guarantees unless customer purchases an enterprise SLA.

Prohibited Use

Any attempt to copy the platform, extract detection rules, or clone functionality is strictly prohibited.

Dual License Model (Open-Core + Commercial)

You can structure SentinelLog like this:

Community Edition (CE)

• Apache 2.0 or MIT
• Basic parsing, simple CLI scanner
• No real-time pipeline
• No ML models
• No cloud dashboard

Enterprise Edition (EE)

• Proprietary license (the one above)
• Real-time Kafka streaming
• Advanced detection models
• Multi-user dashboard
• SOC workflows
• Enterprise support

This is the same model used by:
• Elastic Search
• Redis
• GitLab
• MongoDB

